551:         // window area (client + non-client) itself. We now know that the
552:         // title bar and the window frame is in the non-client area and we
553:         // can set the scope of the client area in this message, so we can
554:         // remove the title bar and the window frame by let the non-client
555:         // area be covered by the client area (because we can't really get
556:         // rid of the non-client area, it will always be there, all we can
557:         // do is to hide it) , which means we should let the client area's
558:         // size the same with the whole window's size. So there is no room
559:         // for the non-client area and then the user won't be able to see it
560:         // again. But how to achieve this? Very easy, just leave lParam (the
561:         // re-calculated client area) untouched. But of course you can
562:         // modify lParam, then the non-client area will be seen and the
563:         // window borders and the window frame will show up. However, things
564:         // are quite different when you try to modify the top margin of the
565:         // client area. DWM will always draw the whole title bar no matter
