581:         // which has the exact same meaning as the `RECT` that is pointed to
582:         // by `lParam` when `wParam` is `FALSE`. The remaining `RECT`s, in
583:         // conjunction with our return value, can
584:         // be used to specify portions of the source and destination window
585:         // rectangles that are valid and should be preserved. We opt not to
586:         // implement an elaborate client-area preservation technique, and
587:         // simply return 0, which means "preserve the entire old client area
588:         // and align it with the upper-left corner of our new client area".
589:         const auto clientRect = ((wParam == FALSE) ? reinterpret_cast<LPRECT>(lParam) : &(reinterpret_cast<LPNCCALCSIZE_PARAMS>(lParam))->rgrc[0]);
